jammeh-returns-2-5-million-to-the-gambia-for-victims-reparations/articleshow/135992099.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-11-22T09:05:00+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">TOI World Desk</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-135992224,imgsize-920684.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[Flatbush Collapse Lawsuit: Tenant alleges landlord ignored cracks; claims remain unproven]]></title><description>&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/136046165.cms" /&gt;<![CDATA[In the wake of a devastating building collapse in Brooklyn that claimed eight lives, a musician has taken legal action against the landlord for ignoring warnings about visible cracks weeks prior. The lawsuit also raises alarms about nearby construction projects lacking proper structural support. Authorities are now probing the oversight of such projects in densely populated neighborhoods, questioning the responsiveness to residents' concerns before the tragic incident occurred.]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/us/a-brooklyn-musician-says-he-photographed-cracks-weeks-before-an-apartment-building-collapsed-and-killed-eight-people-his-new-lawsuit-claims-the-landlord-ignored-his-warnings-as-construction-continued-next-door/articleshow/136046165.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/us/a-brooklyn-musician-says-he-photographed-cracks-weeks-before-an-apartment-building-collapsed-and-killed-eight-people-his-new-lawsuit-claims-the-landlord-ignored-his-warnings-as-construction-continued-next-door/articleshow/136046165.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-11-22T08:05:48+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">TOI World Desk</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-136046283,imgsize-1071465.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[Former US President George Washington's hair sells for $4,000]]></title><description>&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/136066072.cms" /&gt;<![CDATA[At a recent auction, a rare lock of George Washington’s hair sold for an impressive $4,000. This fascinating artifact once belonged to John Gadsby, who shared a meal with Washington shortly before his passing. Gadsby’s granddaughter later cherished the lock alongside a portrait of the first president, making it a remarkable piece of history. Notably, Washington's hair has previously commanded prices nearing $40,000 at auctions, alongside other treasured memorabilia.]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/us/former-us-president-george-washingtons-hair-sells-for-4000/articleshow/136066072.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/us/former-us-president-george-washingtons-hair-sells-for-4000/articleshow/136066072.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-11-22T07:58:53+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">Mahima Sharma</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-136066091,imgsize-36013.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[COP31 Talks Remain Divided: Countries review Turkish draft; climate support remains uncertain]]></title><description>&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/136065827.cms" /&gt;<![CDATA[At the COP31 climate conference in Turkey, urgent last-minute discussions are underway as Turkish officials unveil a draft agreement amid ongoing disputes regarding fossil fuels. Civil groups voice their frustration over the gradual pace of negotiations, demanding swift action on vital climate challenges. Nations most vulnerable to climate change are advocating for enhanced financial support for recovery and adaptation.]]